<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johnson South Reef skirmish</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1988">1988</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Johnson South Reef skirmish was a naval clash on 14 March 1988 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spratly-islands">Spratly Islands</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-china-sea">South China Sea</a> between Chinese and Vietnamese forces. Chinese ships opened fire on Vietnamese troops and transport vessels at the reef, killing 64 Vietnamese, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> took control of several reefs. It remains a key event in the disputes over the Spratlys.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johnson-south-reef-skirmish.jpg" alt="Johnson South Reef skirmish" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RobertJordan from the Vietnamese Wikipedia · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Union_Banks_en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
